  "notes": "The PX3000 (Ultrapatch Pro) is NOT the well-known EPX3000 power amplifier — it is a fully passive 1U, 19\" rackmount 48-point balanced 1/4\" (6.35mm) TRS patchbay with 24 channels x 2 rear jacks (A/B), each rear pair independently switchable (top-mounted per-channel switch) between Normal, Half-Normal, and Thru modes. It requires no external power and has no power connector or inlet (confirmed passive: no power spec listed on manufacturer page or in manual specifications; safety-notice boilerplate re: mains voltage is generic Behringer manual text, not applicable to this unit). Direction is set to \"bidirectional\" for all points because a patchbay jack carries whatever signal direction the connected external gear defines — the patchbay itself has no fixed input/output role. Only the 48 REAR jacks (which wire to external equipment) are listed as physical I/O; the device also has 48 FRONT panel 1/4\" TRS jacks (mirroring the same 24 channels, 2 per channel) used for inserting patch cords to break normal/half-normal routing — these are omitted since they are patch-access points on the same signal paths rather than distinct external connections, though they are physically the same trs-6.35 connector type. Dimensions/weight (483 x 45 x 93mm, 1.8kg, 1U/19\") and full connector spec were cross-confirmed via Thomann's spec table and a ManualsLib-hosted copy of the official Behringer specifications page, since the manufacturer's own product page only listed connector type/count and omitted a full spec table. No connector in this device qualifies for a bandwidth \"grade\" (all analog balanced audio jacks), so grade is omitted throughout. Category/type were mapped to the closest available enum values (audio / Other) since \"patchbay\" is not a listed type.",
